# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ArchDesk — Cursor AI Rules
# Architecture & Design SaaS for Hubbali, Karnataka
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## Project Overview
ArchDesk is a vertical SaaS platform for architecture and interior design
firms in Tier-2 Indian cities (starting Hubbali, Karnataka). Users are
architects, draftsmen, site managers, and their clients.

## Tech Stack (never suggest alternatives)
- Next.js 14 with App Router (TypeScript, strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui for all UI components
- Clerk for authentication and organisation management
- Prisma ORM + Supabase Postgres for database
- Supabase Storage for files (drawings, renders, site photos)
- Zustand for client state, TanStack React Query for server state
- react-hook-form + Zod for all forms and validation
- Razorpay for payments (India-first, UPI support)
- Resend for transactional email
- @react-pdf/renderer for PDF invoice generation
- Vercel for deployment

## Architecture Rules
- Use Server Components by default. Add "use client" ONLY when needed
  (event handlers, hooks, browser APIs, interactivity)
- API routes live in /app/api/ as Next.js Route Handlers
- All DB access goes through Prisma — never raw SQL
- Protect all dashboard routes via Clerk middleware
- Use Supabase RLS for row-level data isolation per firm
- Never expose API keys or secrets in client components

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode — every function, prop, return type must be typed
- Async/await everywhere — never .then() chains
- Try/catch in all server actions and API routes
- Return typed responses: { data, error } pattern
- Named exports for components, default export for pages
- File naming: kebab-case files, PascalCase components
- Co-locate types in /types/index.ts for shared types

## Indian Market Specifics (CRITICAL)
- Currency: INR only — always format as ₹ with Indian numbering
  CORRECT:   ₹1,05,000  (Indian: lakh system)
  INCORRECT: ₹105,000   (Western format — never use)
- Indian number formatter: new Intl.NumberFormat('en-IN', { style:'currency', currency:'INR' })
- Dates: DD/MM/YYYY format throughout the app
- GST: 18% on architecture services — always show GST breakup on invoices
- Phone numbers: 10-digit Indian mobile numbers (+91 prefix)
- Cities: Hubbali, Dharwad, Belgaum (now Belagavi), Davangere, Mysuru

## Domain Knowledge — Architecture Firm Workflow
Project stages (in order):
  CONCEPT → SCHEMATIC → DESIGN_DEV → WORKING_DRAWINGS → EXECUTION → COMPLETED

Drawing types: PLAN | ELEVATION | SECTION | RENDER | BOQ | OTHER
Drawing statuses: PENDING_REVIEW | APPROVED | REVISION_REQUESTED

Billing is milestone-based (tied to project stages):
  - Retainer (on signing)
  - Schematic fee
  - Design development fee
  - Working drawings fee
  - Site supervision fees
  - Completion fee

Lead pipeline stages:
  NEW → CONTACTED → SITE_VISIT → PROPOSAL_SENT → NEGOTIATION → WON → LOST

## Component Patterns
When generating any component:
1. Define TypeScript interface at the top of the file
2. Use shadcn/ui primitives first, build custom only if needed
3. Include Skeleton loading state (use shadcn Skeleton)
4. Include empty state with descriptive message
5. Include error state with retry option
6. Mobile-responsive with Tailwind breakpoints (mobile-first)
7. Add toast notifications (shadcn Sonner) for all user actions

## Folder Conventions
/app/(dashboard)/[feature]/page.tsx     — list/overview page
/app/(dashboard)/[feature]/[id]/page.tsx — detail page
/components/[feature]/[FeatureName].tsx  — feature component
/hooks/use[Feature].ts                   — React Query hooks
/lib/[service].ts                        — service utilities
/types/index.ts                          — shared TypeScript types

## Database Access Pattern
// Always use this pattern for server components
import { db } from "@/lib/db"
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server"

const { userId } = auth()
const user = await db.user.findUnique({ where: { clerkId: userId } })
const data = await db.[model].findMany({
  where: { firmId: user.firmId },  // ALWAYS scope to firmId
  include: { ... }
})

## Naming Conventions
- DB models: PascalCase (Project, Drawing, Invoice)
- Prisma relations: camelCase (project.drawings, user.firm)
- API routes: /api/[resource]/[id] REST style
- Zustand stores: use[Feature]Store (useProjectStore)
- React Query keys: ['projects', firmId] arrays

## When Generating Forms
Always use this stack:
  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof schema>>({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
    defaultValues: { ... }
  })
Include field-level error messages below each input.
Use shadcn FormField, FormItem, FormLabel, FormMessage.

## Security Rules
- Validate Clerk session on every API route
- Check firmId ownership before any DB read/write
- Sanitize file uploads: check MIME type and file size
- Validate Razorpay webhook signatures
- Rate limit public endpoints (client portal)

## Performance
- Use Next.js Image component for all images
- Paginate lists with cursor-based pagination (not offset)
- Use React Query's staleTime: 1000 * 60 for project data
- Compress images client-side before Supabase upload
  (use browser-image-compression package)
